# Cloudflare combines every rule that matches a path rather than letting a
# later one replace an earlier one. So `Cache-Control` is not set here: a
# `no-cache` on `/*` arrives glued to the front of the asset rule below and
# quietly defeats it.
#
# Leaving it unset lets Pages apply its own default to the HTML, which is to
# revalidate — which is what every path serving the same document wants anyway.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# These are named after their contents, so a changed file is a changed name and
# an unchanged one never has to be asked about again.
/*.wasm
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
